A failure to add a service is emitted as an `'error'` event. `'serviceAdd'` carries only the service `uuid`.

The central role scans for peripherals and connects to them. To connect to a peripheral seen in an earlier scan, store its `id` and resolve it again with `retrievePeripherals()`, which needs no scan. The central has to be powered on first, because the call throws otherwise.

```js
const bluetooth = require('bare-bluetooth-apple')

const savedId = '9D1F6A4C-0F3B-4E5A-8A52-5F3A8B7C1D20' // a peripheral.id stored by your app

const central = new bluetooth.Central()

central.on('stateChange', (state) => {
  if (state !== 'poweredOn') return

  const [peripheral] = central.retrievePeripherals([savedId])

  if (peripheral) central.connect(peripheral)
})

central.on('connect', (peripheral) => {
  peripheral.discoverServices()
})

central.on('error', (err) => {
  console.error('central error:', err.code, err.message)
})
